# Signs cookies and derives verification/state tokens; generate a long random value (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) and set it on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`, never commit the real value. The placeholder below is deliberately short and obviously fake — it fails createAuth's own guard (must be present, must not be Better Auth's public default, must be at least 32 characters) if pasted in verbatim.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=CHANGE-ME-not-a-real-secret

# Public origin of the site that owns the Better Auth session (e.g. https://admin.illith.com in production); set on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`. Also what `invitations.ts`'s `sendInvitationEmail` builds the `/accept-invite?token=…` link from — unset, that scheduled function throws (visible as a failed job in the dashboard) rather than silently sending nothing.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Both variables above are only required for auth instances that serve HTTP
# requests (convex/http.ts's createAuth call, which runs on the app deployment
# where these are set). Regenerating the Better Auth schema does NOT require
# either variable: convex/betterAuth/auth.ts is an introspection-only shim for
# the schema generator — it is never reachable as a Convex function and never
# serves a request — and it explicitly opts out with `createAuth({} as any,
# { requireSecret: false })`. That is the only place in the codebase allowed
# to do so (`grep -rn "requireSecret: false" packages/backend` must return
# exactly that one line); every other call goes through the default, which
# throws rather than letting better-auth fall back to its publicly-known
# default secret.

# HMAC key for preview-page tokens (design spec §6.3; `convex/lib/previewToken.ts`). Signs and re-verifies `{type}:{id}:{expiresAt}` for `previewPage` — the only thing standing between a draft page and anyone who guesses or leaks a preview URL, since `apps/web` carries no session at all. Generate a real value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) and set it on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`, never commit the real value. Also shared, unchanged, with the `web` container's own independent verification of the same token (Task 7) — generate it once, set it in both places. The placeholder below is deliberately short and obviously fake — `verifyPreviewToken`/`signPreviewToken` throw rather than silently degrading if it's pasted in verbatim (must be present, must be at least 32 characters).
PREVIEW_SECRET=CHANGE-ME-not-a-real-secret

# Resend API key used by `invitations.ts` to send invitation emails (via `@convex-dev/resend`). Left unset, `resend.sendEmail` throws "API key is not set" from inside the *scheduled* send — never from `invitations.create` itself, so a missing key never voids the invitation, only the email. Get one at https://resend.com; set on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`, never commit the real value.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The Resend component's own safe default is `testMode: true`, which only allows delivery to Resend's test addresses (e.g. delivered@resend.dev) — a guard rail so a misconfigured dev/staging deployment can't spam real inboxes. `invitations.ts` reads this var as `!== "false"`, so anything other than the literal string "false" (including unset) keeps that default. Set to `false` — and configure a verified sending domain in the Resend dashboard first — to actually deliver invitation emails in production.
RESEND_TEST_MODE=true
